# The root container of this server: the public may read it (the welcome
# page, index.html), nobody may write to it through HTTP. Each pod has its own
# .acl and is not affected. The image copies this file over stock CSS's
# templates/root/intro/wac/.acl (Dockerfile), which initialize-intro.json
# writes on first start only.
#
# Why not the stock one: it gives foaf:Agent Read, Write, Append and Control on
# <./> with acl:default, and its header says "DO NOT USE UNMODIFIED UNLESS FOR
# TESTING PURPOSES". On two live instances (2026-11-23) scanners had POSTed
# exploit probes into the root, and anyone could have replaced the welcome page
# or this very file. The welcome page needs no HTTP write: start/welcome.js puts
# it in the data from the filesystem.
#
# An instance created before this image keeps the root .acl it has:
# docs/root-acl.md says how to replace it.

@prefix acl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#>.
@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>.

<#public>
    a               acl:Authorization;
    acl:agentClass  foaf:Agent;
    acl:mode        acl:Read;
    acl:accessTo    <./>;
    acl:default     <./>.
